     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">20% reduction in the number of affected people (experienced)

20% of the target population with adequate WASH services and higiene practices</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="ES">Four main results have been planned: 
R1. Affected vulnerable rural indigenous populations and local
governments improved their preparedness capacities to cope with future events; 
R2. Populations using the
water systems access safe drinking water and operational improvements on the Water Boards&#x2019; enhanced
capacities. 
R3. Urgent early recovery actions in support of livelihoods in rural communities are undertaken;
R4. Improved management of information allowing indigenous communities to better understand hazards
and risks they are vulnerable to. 
R5. Crisis modifiers - Emergency Assistance.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
